{#-
    Every `{% if %}` left in this file is logic. None of them is a default.

    Fourteen were: `{%-if element.x %}...{% else %}<value>{% endif-%}` pairs
    holding #FFFFFF, 16px, border-radius 0px, height auto, padding 0px and the
    rest. component/button.js declares all of them now, so each collapsed to
    `{{ element.x }}`. Proven rather than assumed -- every one of the fourteen
    had its value replaced with a unique sentinel, all nine golden cases were
    built, and none of the sentinels reached the output.

    What remains, and why it is not a default:

      - `element.mode` branches. An underline or outline button is a different
        shape, not a button missing a value: no fill, no stroke, tighter
        margins, and a coloured bottom border. Six of them, five inside the
        Outlook block.
      - `element.border_*`. These fall back to another property rather than to
        a literal -- an unset border takes the button's background -- so there
        is nothing to move into the library.
      - `element.background` and `element.font_weight`, which are emitted or
        not. No value to default to.
      - `element.force_mso_colour`, which suppresses a declaration rather than
        supplying one.

    The Outlook half is load-bearing and deliberately untouched. VML wants its
    own attributes -- arcsize, fillcolor, strokecolor, strokeweight -- and
    `<v:roundrect>` needs an explicit height, which is what `mso_height` is for
    and why it is a separate key from `height`. The conditional comments must
    stay comments: every other client ignores what is between them.

    This file has no trailing newline. It is included once per button, so one
    would put a blank line after every button in the output.
-#}
<div class="acr-fragment acr-component {{ element.custom_class }}" data-component-id="button:2" style="width: 100%;text-align: {{ element.align }}; " contenteditable="false" data-lock-type="editable" data-source-uuid="aers-button-component" data-has-int-mso-hack="true">
